  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-git",
      "text": "A DSH plugin that adds a **Git** page to the right sidebar: the working tree's changes and the\nrecent commits on one side, and the diff a click opens on the other — read-only, highlighted,\nside by side. The list stays where it is, so two diffs can be put beside each other.\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n| Two columns, wrapped | Two columns, unwrapped | One column |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Needs Node 22.19+ (or 24+) and the DSH CLI.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @lengmoxxl/dsh-git\ndsh --profile web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements, permissions, and limits",
      "text": "- A `git` executable on `PATH`, and a Git working tree as the session's working directory.\n- Reads that repository through the Harness filesystem and runs `git` through the Harness subprocess: no network, no credentials, no other path.\n- Writes nothing — not the tree, not the index. Commands run with the DSH process's own privileges, and a large repository or diff takes time to gather and draw."
    },
    {
      "section": "Release",
      "text": "From a clean `main`:\n\n```sh\nnpm version patch -m \"Cut %s\"   # or minor / major\nnpm publish\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
